 Aim for a ",[262,267,268],{},"portable Core"," and treat Extended as best-effort.",[258,271,272,279],{},[273,274],"img",{"alt":275,"className":276,"src":278},"Core elements versus extended best-effort elements",[277],"dark:hidden","\u002Fillustrations\u002Ftiers.light.svg",[273,280],{"alt":275,"className":281,"src":284},[282,283],"hidden","dark:block","\u002Fillustrations\u002Ftiers.dark.svg",[286,287,289],"h2",{"id":288},"core","Core",[258,291,292,294,295,298,299,303,304,307,308,311],{},[262,293,289],{}," means the element is present on every matrix platform and keeps its IR semantics (layout role, text, tap target, bitmap image, …). It does ",[262,296,297],{},"not"," mean identical pixels. Degraded cells (for example Windows ",[300,301,302],"code",{},"zstack"," \u002F ",[300,305,306],{},"shape",", or ",[300,309,310],{},"image.systemName"," outside Apple) are documented in the matrix below — check them before assuming Board\u002FGlance look like WidgetKit.",[258,313,314,315,318,319,322,323,328],{},"The authoritative list is ",[300,316,317],{},"CORE_ELEMENTS"," in ",[300,320,321],{},"src\u002Fsnapshot.rs"," (also mirrored under ",[324,325,327],"a",{"href":326},"#capability-matrix","Capability matrix","). Prefer that set when you need broad coverage.",[330,331,333],"h3",{"id":332},"portable-core-checklist","Portable Core checklist",[335,336,337,341,354,360],"ul",{},[338,339,340],"li",{},"Prefer solid backgrounds (or accept gradient bake \u002F first-stop degradation).",[338,342,343,344,303,347,350,351,353],{},"Prefer ",[300,345,346],{},"image.data",[300,348,349],{},"image.url"," over ",[300,352,310],{}," for Board\u002FAndroid parity — SF Symbols exist only on Apple; elsewhere the feature row is degraded (glyph\u002Femoji).",[338,355,356,357,359],{},"Remote ",[300,358,349],{}," is prefetched on the host where wired — do not rely on live network inside the extension process.",[338,361,362],{},"Prefer Desktop webview when you need true overlays, live timers, or full SVG canvas.",[286,364,366],{"id":365},"extended","Extended",[258,368,369,371,372,375,376,379,380,383,384,387],{},[262,370,366],{}," (",[300,373,374],{},"EXTENDED_ELEMENTS",") is best-effort and platform-dependent. Expect ",[300,377,378],{},"degraded"," or ",[300,381,382],{},"unsupported"," cells (live ",[300,385,386],{},"timer"," on Windows Board, chart rasterization on Adaptive Cards). The live list is in the matrix section.",[286,389,391],{"id":390},"how-to-read-the-matrix","How to read the matrix",[393,394,395,408],"table",{},[396,397,398],"thead",{},[399,400,401,405],"tr",{},[402,403,404],"th",{},"Level",[402,406,407],{},"Meaning",[409,410,411,420,427],"tbody",{},[399,412,413,417],{},[414,415,416],"td",{},"full",[414,418,419],{},"Supported with the intended semantics",[399,421,422,424],{},[414,423,378],{},[414,425,426],{},"Renders with known limitations (see footnotes under the matrix)",[399,428,429,431],{},[414,430,382],{},[414,432,433],{},"Do not rely on this feature on that platform",[258,435,436,439,440,443,444,447,448,451],{},[262,437,438],{},"Desktop column:"," one IR path shared by the desktop webview hosts — WKWebView (macOS window), WebView2 (Windows window), and webkit2gtk (Linux). Semantics match; differences are system fonts and CSS engine version. Linux also has its own golden stand (",[300,441,442],{},"tests\u002Fgolden\u002Flinux\u002F",") for pinning \u002F layer-shell, but it is not a sixth matrix column. Windows ",[262,445,446],{},"Widgets Board"," (Adaptive Cards) is the separate ",[262,449,450],{},"Windows"," column.",[258,453,454],{},"Showcase presets exercise both tiers.",[286,456,458],{"id":457},"runtime-behavior","Runtime behavior",[330,460,462,463],{"id":461},"capability-warnings-on-setwidgetconfig","Capability warnings on ",[300,464,465],{},"setWidgetConfig",[258,467,468,469,471,472,475,476,479,480,483,484,303,486,488,489,491],{},"Each ",[300,470,465],{}," runs ",[300,473,474],{},"validate_config"," for the current host platform and emits ",[300,477,478],{},"log::warn!"," via ",[300,481,482],{},"log_capabilities"," when a used element or feature is ",[300,485,378],{},[300,487,382],{}," (for example ",[300,490,310],{}," outside Apple). Warnings are advisory — the write still proceeds. There is no public guest API to dry-run validation yet; treat host logs (and the matrix) as the source of truth before shipping a config.",[330,493,495],{"id":494},"skipped-elements-in-render-receipts","Skipped elements in render receipts",[258,497,498,499,502,503,506],{},"When a renderer cannot express a node (common on Adaptive Cards without the ",[300,500,501],{},"rasterize"," feature, or after a flatten), the element is recorded on the render receipt as ",[300,504,505],{},"skipped: [{ type, reason }]",", not as a silent hole you must guess about.",[258,508,509,510,515],{},"Inspect recent receipts with ",[324,511,512],{"href":179},[300,513,514],{},"getWidgetDiagnostics(group)",":",[517,518,523],"pre",{"className":519,"code":520,"language":521,"meta":522,"style":522},"language-ts shiki shiki-themes material-theme-lighter material-theme material-theme-palenight","import { getWidgetDiagnostics } from \"tauri-plugin-widgets-api\";\n\nconst receipts = await getWidgetDiagnostics(\"com.example.widgets\");\nfor (const r of receipts) {\n  if (r.skipped?.length) {\n    console.warn(r.widgetId, r.skipped);\n    \u002F\u002F e.g. [{ type: \"canvas\", reason: \"adaptive-cards: enable crate feature `rasterize`\" }]\n  }\n}\n","ts","",[300,524,525,561,568,602,624,653,687,694,700],{"__ignoreMap":522},[526,527,530,534,538,542,545,548,551,555,558],"span",{"class":528,"line":529},"line",1,[526,531,533],{"class":532},"s7zQu","import",[526,535,537],{"class":536},"sMK4o"," {",[526,539,541],{"class":540},"sTEyZ"," getWidgetDiagnostics",[526,543,544],{"class":536}," }",[526,546,547],{"class":532}," from",[526,549,550],{"class":536}," \"",[526,552,554],{"class":553},"sfazB","tauri-plugin-widgets-api",[526,556,557],{"class":536},"\"",[526,55